pe":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#bonus-items-hidden-rewards","content":"Bonus items are given server-side when the reward is claimed. Players will see them appear in their inventory but won't see them during the roll animation."},"1215":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/examples-21","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#custom-reward-types-with-hooks","content":"Use custom reward types to handle non-item rewards like vehicles or bank deposits. Register hooks in your own resource to handle these reward types."},"1216":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/examples-22","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#lootbox-config-with-custom-rewards","content":"If a custom `rewardType` is set but no hook is registered, the system will log a warning and fall back to treating it as a regular item. This prevents rewards from being lost but may not give the intended reward."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/examples-23","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/examples#removing-a-hook","content":"You can remove a previously registered hook if needed:"},"1218":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"page","content":"Framework Setup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Free Resources","Lootbox"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup"},"1219":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-0","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works","content":"How It Works"},"1220":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-1","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#ox_core--ox_inventory-setup","content":"ox_core + ox_inventory Setup"},"1221":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-2","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"Item Definition Format"},"1222":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-3","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"How It Works (ox_core)"},"1223":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-4","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Complete Example"},"1224":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-5","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order","content":"Resource Order"},"1225":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-6","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#qbcore--qbox-setup","content":"QBCore / Qbox Setup"},"1226":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-7","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"Item Definition Format"},"1227":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-8","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"How It Works (QBCore / Qbox)"},"1228":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-9","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example-1","content":"Complete Example"},"1229":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-10","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order-1","content":"Resource Order"},"1230":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-11","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#reference-file","content":"Reference File"},"1231":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-12","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#adding-custom-lootboxes","content":"Adding Custom Lootboxes"},"1232":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-13","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1233":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-14","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"Item does nothing when used"},"1234":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-15","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#no-supported-framework-detected-warning","content":"\"No supported framework detected\" warning"},"1235":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-16","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#lootbox-opens-but-no-item-is-given","content":"Lootbox opens but no item is given"},"1236":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-17","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","content":"Each framework handles usable items differently. This page explains how to configure your item definitions so that lootbox cases work correctly with your framework and inventory system."},"1237":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-18","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","content":"These steps are **in addition** to defining your lootboxes in `config.lua`. You must also ensure the item definitions exist in your inventory/framework so players can hold and use the items."},"1238":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-19","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works","content":"When `config.registerUsableItems = true` (the default), sleepless\\_lootbox automatically registers each lootbox as a usable item through the framework bridge. However, the item must still be **defined** in your inventory or framework's item list — the resource can only register the *use callback*, not create the item definition itself."},"1239":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-20","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#ox_core--ox_inventory-setup","content":"When using **ox\\_core**, usable items are handled through **ox\\_inventory** item definitions rather than the framework itself. For each lootbox case item, you need to add a `server.export` entry in your ox\\_inventory item definitions that points back to this resource."},"1240":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-21","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `ox_inventory/data/items.lua`:"},"1241":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-22","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format","content":"The `server.export` value **must** follow the format `sleepless_lootbox.<item_name>`, where `<item_name>` matches the lootbox key defined in your `config.lua` or registered via exports. Without this, using the item will do nothing."},"1242":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-23","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"ox\\_inventory sees that the item has a `server.export` defined."},"1243":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-24","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"When a player uses the item, ox\\_inventory calls the matching export on `sleepless_lootbox`."},"1244":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-25","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The ox framework bridge registers these exports automatically when `config.registerUsableItems = true`."},"1245":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-26","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-ox_core","content":"The lootbox opens for the player."},"1246":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-27","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Here are all three default lootbox cases configured for ox\\_inventory:"},"1247":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-28","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example","content":"Don't forget to also add item definitions for any **loot contents** (weapons, items, etc.) that your lootboxes can reward. Those items don't need `server.export` — only the case items do."},"1248":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-29","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order","content":"Make sure your `server.cfg` starts resources in the correct order:"},"1249":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-30","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#qbcore--qbox-setup","content":"When using **QBCore** or **Qbox**, lootbox case items must be defined in your shared items table with `useable = true`. This allows the framework to register usable item callbacks."},"1250":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-31","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"Add your lootbox case items to `qb-core/shared/items.lua`:"},"1251":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-32","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-definition-format-1","content":"The `useable = true` flag is **required**. Without it, `QBCore.Functions.CreateUseableItem` (or `exports.qbx_core:CreateUseableItem` for Qbox) will not be able to register the callback, and using the item will do nothing."},"1252":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-33","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"The framework sees that the item has `useable = true` in the shared items table."},"1253":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-34","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"When `config.registerUsableItems = true`, the bridge calls `CreateUseableItem` for each lootbox."},"1254":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-35","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"When a player uses the item, the framework triggers the registered callback."},"1255":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-36","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#how-it-works-qbcore--qbox","content":"The lootbox opens for the player."},"1256":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-37","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example-1","content":"Here are all three default lootbox cases configured for QBCore/Qbox:"},"1257":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-38","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#complete-example-1","content":"Don't forget to also add item definitions for any **loot contents** (weapons, items, etc.) that your lootboxes can reward. Those items don't need `useable = true` — only the case items do."},"1258":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-39","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order-1","content":"Make sure your `server.cfg` starts resources in the correct order:"},"1259":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-40","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#resource-order-1","content":"For Qbox, replace `qb-core` with `qbx_core`:"},"1260":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-41","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#reference-file","content":"The resource includes a `_items.lua` reference file in its root directory containing example item definitions for both ox\\_inventory and QBCore/Qbox. This file is **not loaded at runtime** — it's purely for reference. Copy the relevant entries into your framework's item configuration."},"1261":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-42","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#adding-custom-lootboxes","content":"When you register a new lootbox (either in `config.lua` or via the `registerLootbox` export), you need to add a matching item definition to your framework:"},"1262":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-43","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**ox\\_inventory:** Verify the item definition includes `server.export = \"sleepless_lootbox.<item_name>\"` and that the item name matches your lootbox key exactly."},"1263":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**QBCore/Qbox:** Verify the item definition has `useable = true` in the shared items table."},"1264":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**All frameworks:** Ensure `config.registerUsableItems = true` in your `config.lua`."},"1265":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-46","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#item-does-nothing-when-used","content":"**All frameworks:** Ensure `sleepless_lootbox` starts **after** your framework and inventory in `server.cfg`."},"1266":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-47","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#no-supported-framework-detected-warning","content":"Check that your framework resource is started before `sleepless_lootbox`. The bridge auto-detects the framework by checking if the resource is started, so load order matters."},"1267":{"id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup-48","page_id":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/lootbox/framework-setup#lootbox-opens-but-no-item-is-given","content":"This is likely an inventory bridge issue. Make sure the loot content items (not the case items) are also defined in your inventory system. The resource can only give items that your inventory recognizes."},"1268":{"id":"/docs/lootbox","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"page","content":"Sleepless Lootbox","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Free Resources","Lootbox"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox"},"1269":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-0","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#features","content":"Features"},"1270":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-1","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#dependencies","content":"Dependencies"},"1271":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-2","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#installation","content":"Installation"},"1272":{"id":"/docs/lootbox-3","page_id":"/docs/lootbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/lootbox#down